The proposed answer is incorrect. Jean Boucicaut (Jean II Le Maingre) was a Marshal of France present at Agincourt, but he was not the Constable, he did not hold overall command, and he was not killed — he was captured and later died in England in 1421.

The Constable of France in 1415 was Charles d'Albret, Count of Dreux. He held overall command of the French army at Agincourt and was killed in the battle.

