The proposed answer is wrong. While the Potemkin did visit Odessa early in the mutiny (June 1905), the crew did not surrender the ship there — Odessa was a Russian port, so there were no foreign consular authorities to take custody of a warship there. After Odessa, the mutineers sailed to several other ports hoping for support (Constanta was briefly considered), and eventually sailed to Romania. On July 8 (O.S. June 25), 1905, the Potemkin entered the Romanian port of Constanța, where the crew surrendered the ship to the Romanian authorities. Romanian sailors later returned the ship to the Russian government.

So the correct answer is Constanța (Constanza), Romania, not Odessa.

